BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (2. The display shows the firmware version \(3.4.1 for instruments shipped from June 2025\), the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (   serial number and the instrument name.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (3. The display shows the alarm set points for each gas in turn.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (4. The display shows the days remaining until the next calibration and the next bump test. If) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (   either is overdue, the yellow LED lights and "CAL DUE" or "BUMP DUE" is shown.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (5. The sensors warm up for 45 seconds. The LEL sensor may read slightly negative during) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 651 Td (   warm-up; this is normal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 638 Td (6. The instrument enters measuring mode. Perform a fresh-air zero \(section 8\) if the readings) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 625 Td (   are not zero in clean air.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 609 Td (6. Display and navigation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 587 Td (In measuring mode the display shows four readings in a two-by-two grid: O2 \(top left\), LEL \(top) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 574 Td (right\), CO \(bottom left\) and H2S \(bottom right\). The status bar at the top shows battery level,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 561 Td (time, and icons for datalogging and docking.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 539 Td (To enter the user menu, press UP and DOWN together for 2 seconds. The user menu contains:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 517 Td (- Menu > Peak Readings: shows and clears peak readings since power-on.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 504 Td (- Menu > Bump Test: starts a manual bump test.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 491 Td (- Menu > Zero: performs a fresh-air zero of O2, LEL, CO and H2S.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 478 Td (- Menu > Instrument: shows serial number, firmware version, battery health and the Service) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 465 Td (   submenu.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 452 Td (- Menu > Settings: display contrast, language, time format and backlight timeout \(default 15) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 439 Td (   seconds\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 426 Td (- Menu > Supervisor: protected by the supervisor passcode \(see section 12\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 413 Td (The menu closes automatically after 30 seconds without a button press and returns to measuring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 400 Td (mode. The instrument continues to monitor gas and will alarm while any menu is open.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 375 Td (7. Alarms) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 353 Td (The HX-210 has five types of gas alarm: low, high, STEL \(short-term exposure limit, 15-minute) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 340 Td (rolling average\), TWA \(time-weighted average, 8-hour\) and over-range. O2 has low and high) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 327 Td (alarms only, because oxygen is hazardous both when deficient and when enriched.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 305 Td (Factory default set points for the HX-210:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 284 Td (Gas | Low alarm | High alarm | STEL | TWA) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 272 Td (H2S | 5 ppm | 10 ppm | 15 ppm | 5 ppm) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 260 Td (CO | 30 ppm | 100 ppm | 200 ppm | 30 ppm) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 248 Td (LEL \(CH4\) | 10% LEL | 20% LEL | n/a | n/a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 236 Td (O2 | 19.5% vol \(falling\) | 23.0% vol \(rising\) | n/a | n/a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 214 Td (Alarm behaviour:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 192 Td (- Low alarm: slow two-tone sound, slow red flash, pulsed vibration. Non-latching by default;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 179 Td (   the alarm clears when the reading falls below the set point.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 166 Td (- High alarm: fast sound, fast red flash, continuous vibration. Latching; the alarm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 153 Td (   continues after the gas clears until the user presses ON/OK in clean air.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 140 Td (- STEL and TWA alarms: latching, and cannot be acknowledged until the instrument is switched) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 127 Td (   off. Leave the area and inform your supervisor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 114 Td (- Over-range: the display shows "OR" and the high alarm operates. For LEL, an over-range) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 101 Td (   reading latches the LEL channel out of service until the instrument is switched off and on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 88 Td (   in clean air, to protect the catalytic sensor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 75 Td (Set points can be changed only in the supervisor menu \(Menu > Supervisor > Alarms > Set Points\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 62 Td (or with Meridian Link. Do not set the O2 high alarm above 23.5% vol or the LEL high alarm above) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
