stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (60% LEL; the instrument will reject values outside the certified limits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 707 Td (Low battery warning: at approximately 30 minutes of runtime remaining, the instrument beeps) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 694 Td (once a minute and shows "BATT LOW". At approximately 5 minutes remaining it shows "BATT OFF") Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 681 Td (and switches itself off after a 60-second countdown.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 656 Td (8. Fresh-air zero and bump testing) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 633 Td (8.1 Fresh-air zero) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 611 Td (Perform a fresh-air zero whenever the instrument is switched on in clean air and readings are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 598 Td (not zero \(or 20.9% for O2\). Select Menu > Zero and confirm with ON/OK. The zero takes 30) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 585 Td (seconds. Do not zero in an area where gas may be present.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 562 Td (8.2 Bump test) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 540 Td (A bump test confirms that each sensor responds to gas and each alarm operates. Bump test the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 527 Td (HX-210 before each day's use.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 505 Td (The bump test can be performed in the HX-DOCK-4 \(automatic, recommended\) or manually:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 483 Td (1. Fit the calibration cap HX-CAP-210 and connect the hose to an MI-REG-10 regulator on a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 470 Td (   cylinder of MI-CAL-Q4-B.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 457 Td (2. Select Menu > Bump Test and confirm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 444 Td (3. Open the regulator. Gas flows at 1.0 L/min.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 431 Td (4. The bump test passes if each sensor reaches at least 80% of the cylinder concentration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 418 Td (   within 45 seconds and the alarms operate. O2 must fall to 18.0% vol plus or minus 0.5.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 405 Td (5. Close the regulator, remove the cap and allow the readings to return to normal before use.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 392 Td (If any sensor fails the bump test, calibrate the instrument \(section 9\). If the sensor still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 379 Td (fails, replace it following sup-hx-sensor-replacement-procedure.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 354 Td (9. Calibration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 332 Td (The HX-210 must be calibrated at least every 120 days. This interval was reduced from 180 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 319 Td (in May 2025 following analysis of field data showing LEL sensitivity drift. The instrument) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 306 Td (counts down the days to the next calibration and displays "CAL DUE" when the interval expires.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 293 Td (The interval is set to 120 days at the factory from firmware 3.4.1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 271 Td (Calibration uses MI-CAL-Q4-B \(1.1% vol CH4 equivalent to 25% LEL, 18.0% O2, 50 ppm CO and 15) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 258 Td (ppm H2S, balance nitrogen\) at 1.0 L/min through the MI-REG-10 regulator. The full step-by-step) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 245 Td (method, including the span stabilisation wait of 120 seconds, is in the controlled document) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 232 Td (HX-210 Calibration Procedure, document ID prod-hx210-calibration-procedure-v2. Always follow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 219 Td (the current version of that procedure. Version 1 of the procedure \(180-day interval,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 206 Td (MI-CAL-Q4-A\) is withdrawn.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 184 Td (Calibration in the HX-DOCK-4 is recommended because it records the result automatically and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 171 Td (prints or exports a certificate. The dock must be running dock firmware D-2.1.0 or later to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 158 Td (calibrate instruments on firmware 3.4.1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 136 Td (If calibration fails, the instrument shows E-104 \(span calibration failed\). See section 13 and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 123 Td (the Halcyon Error Code Reference.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 98 Td (10. Datalogging and Meridian Link) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 76 Td (The HX-210 logs readings from all four sensors at a 1-minute interval by default. At a 1-minute) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 63 Td (interval the datalog holds approximately 90 days of continuous operation, after which the) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
