BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (oldest data is overwritten. The interval can be set between 1 second and 15 minutes in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (supervisor menu \(Menu > Supervisor > Datalog > Interval\). If overwriting is disabled, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (instrument shows E-140 \(datalog memory full\) when the log is full.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 681 Td (The event log records the last 500 events, including alarms, bump tests, calibrations, faults) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668 Td (and power cycles, with a time stamp.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 646 Td (To download the datalog, dock the instrument in the HX-DOCK-4 or connect it by USB-C to a PC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 633 Td (running Meridian Link version 4.2 or later. In Meridian Link, select Instruments > Download) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 620 Td (Logs. Data can be exported as CSV or as a PDF exposure report.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 598 Td (The real-time clock is set automatically when the instrument is docked. If the clock is lost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 585 Td (\(for example after the battery has been removed for more than 72 hours\), the instrument shows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 572 Td (E-126 and must be docked or connected to Meridian Link to set the time.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 547 Td (11. Maintenance) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 524 Td (11.1 Cleaning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 502 Td (Clean the housing with a damp cloth and mild detergent only. Do not use solvents,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 489 Td (silicone-based polishes or alcohol wipes near the sensor grille; these can poison the LEL) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 476 Td (sensor or damage the dust membrane. Do not immerse the instrument deliberately, although it is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 463 Td (rated IP67.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 440 Td (11.2 Dust membrane) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 418 Td (The sensor grille is protected by a hydrophobic dust membrane, part number HX-MEM-210. Inspect) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 405 Td (the membrane weekly. Replace it every 6 months, or immediately if it is visibly dirty, torn or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 392 Td (wet. A blocked membrane causes slow response and may cause a bump test failure.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 369 Td (11.3 Checking sensor life) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 347 Td (The instrument estimates the remaining life of each sensor from its sensitivity at the last) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 334 Td (calibration. To view it, select Menu > Instrument > Service > Sensor Life. Each sensor is shown) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 321 Td (with a percentage. Plan to replace a sensor when its remaining life falls below 20%. The O2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 308 Td (sensor typically lasts 24 to 30 months; the LEL, CO and H2S sensors typically last 36 months in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 295 Td (normal use.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 272 Td (11.4 Opening the housing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 250 Td (The rear housing is held by six captive Torx T10 screws. Open the housing only in a safe area,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 237 Td (with the instrument switched off, to replace the battery pack or sensors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 215 Td (When refitting the rear housing, tighten the six Torx T10 screws in a diagonal pattern to 0.45) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 202 Td (N m. Do not exceed 0.5 N m; over-tightening can crack the screw bosses and invalidate the IP67) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 189 Td (rating. Check that the rear gasket, part number HX-GSK-210, is seated in its groove and is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 176 Td (twisted. Replace the gasket every time a sensor is replaced or if it shows any cut or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 163 Td (compression set.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 140 Td (11.5 Replacing the battery pack) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 118 Td (1. Switch off the instrument and move to a safe area.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 105 Td (2. Remove the six rear housing screws and lift off the rear housing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 92 Td (3. Disconnect the HX-BAT-210 connector by pulling the connector body, not the wires.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 79 Td (4. Fit the new HX-BAT-210, route the wires in the channel and refit the rear housing as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 66 Td (   described in 11.4.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
